-documents/spl_1H31MW3T81S0R67B/prj_1JN6XNWDQ1S0BSN7/pjd_1K88SPJPW1S0RN5Y/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"Project Design Document | 28 Feb 2025\"},{\"h\":\"/ghg-entry/rmv_1KXKP77Q21S08Q74?tab=calculation-view\",\"t\":\"See GHG entry →\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H31MW3T81S0R67B/prj_1JN6XNWDQ1S0BSN7/pjd_1M2115N8N1S00E70/verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H31MW3T81S0R67B/prj_1JN6XNWDQ1S0BSN7/pjd_1M2115DDA1S0S4FP/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H31MW3T81S0R67B/prj_1JN6XNWDQ1S0BSN7/pjd_1KJCPX3AJ1S02GAG/project_name_change_confirmation.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H31MW3T81S0R67B/prj_1JN6XNWDQ1S0BSN7/pjd_1KGFFS4CJ1S04HBE/verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H31MW3T81S0R67B/prj_1JN6XNWDQ1S0BSN7/pjd_1KGFFPSXJ1S0523X/ghg_statement.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nBICRS\\n200Y+\\nCharm Range & Plains Biochar\\nCharm Industrial\\nISSUED\\n101.03\\nBUFFER POOL\\n2.042\\nCREDITING PERIOD\\n01 Mar 2024 to 01 Mar 2029\\nSummary\\nRemoval method\\nCalculation overview\\nProject documentation\\nCertificates\\nReversal risk\\nSummary\\n\\nCharm co-produces bio-oil and biochar at our pyrolysis facility in Fort Lupton, CO from non-merchantable woody biomass sourced from government-funded wildfire mitigation/management projects. Charm procures pyrolysis bio-oil produced by AE Cote-Nord Canada Bioenergy Inc (AECN) from waste material produced by a nearby lumber mill. We transport biochar via truck to various sites where it is sequestered via land application. Charm is in the process of securing agreements for offtake and storage of biochar. The locations of storage sites are presently unknown. Charm will report storage site locations and boundaries upon successful execution of an offtake agreement.\\n\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nCurrent verifier\\n350Solutions\\n->\\nProject code\\n6TMZ\\nApproval date\\n04 Aug 2025\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.0\\nAccreditation\\nSUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT GOALS\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nCharm Range & Plains Biochar\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nProject Design Document\\n28 Feb 2025\\nCalculation overview\\nCalculations demonstrating 0.53 tCO₂e removed from Charm Range & Plains Biochar on 06 Jun 2026\\nSee GHG entry →\\nNet CO₂e Removed\\n526 kg\\nSequestrations\\n980 kg\\n+\\nAdjustments\\n13 kgCO₂e\\n-\\nActivities\\n467 kgCO₂e\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nView full screen\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n08 Sep 2026\\tVerification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n08 Sep 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n26 Feb 2026\\tProject Name Change Confirmation\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n02 Feb 2026\\tVerification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n02 Feb 2026\\tGHG Statement\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 5 of 9\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nCertificates\\nIssued\\n101.03\\nRetired\\n3.449\\nBuffer pool\\n2.042\\nCrediting period\\n01 Mar 2024 to 01 Mar 2029\\nIssuances\\nRetirements\\nIssue date\\tIssued\\tBuffer pool\\tSupplier allocation\\n08 Sep 2026\\t49.78\\t1.009\\t48.771\\n02 Feb 2026\\t47.73\\t0.962\\t46.768\\n04 Aug 2025\\t3.52\\t0.071\\t3.449\\nShowing 3 of 3\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nReversal risk\\n\\nThe risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 2% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to Charm Industrial's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 2.042 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 317.85 certificates.\\n\\nCharm Industrial has no reversals to date.\\n\\nLearn more about reversal risk\"}"